G2193.def:
**ἕως**,
_relative particle_ (Lat. _donee, usque), _
expressing the terminus ad quem (cf. Burton, §321ff.).
I. As _conjunction_;
1. **till, until**;
(a) of a fact in past time, with indic.: [[Mat.2.9|Mat.2:9]], al. ([[Wis.10.14|Wis.10:14]], al.);
(b) ἕως ἄν, with subjc. aor.: [[Mat.2.13; 5.18|Mat.2:13 5:18]], [[Mrk.6.10|Mrk.6:10]], al.; without ἄν (M. _Pr._, 168f.; Lft., _Notes_, 115), [[Mrk.14.32|Mrk.14:32]] (Burton, §325), [[Luk.12.59|Luk.12:59]], [[2Th.2.7|2Th.2:7]], al.;
(with) with indic., present (Burton, §328; BL, §65, 10): [[Mrk.6.45|Mrk.6:45]], [[Jhn.21.22, 23|Jhn.21:22, 23]] [[1Ti.4.13|1Ti.4:13]].
2. C. indic., **as long as, while** (Burton, §327): [[Jhn.9.4|Jhn.9:4]] (Plat., Phaedo, 89c).
II. As an _adverb_ (chiefly in late writers).
1. Of time, **until, unto**;
(a) as _prep._ with genitive (BL, §40, 6; M, _Pr._, 99): τ. ἡμέρας, [[Mat.26.29|Mat.26:29]], [[Luk.1.80|Luk.1:80]], [[Rom.11.8|Rom.11:8]], al.; ὥρας, [[Mat.27.45|Mat.27:45]], al.; τέλους, [[1Co.1.8|1Co.1:8]], [[2Co.1.13|2Co.1:13]]; τ. νῦν, [[Mat.24.21|Mat.24:21]], [[Mrk.13.19|Mrk.13:19]] ([[1Ma.2.33|1Ma.2:33]]); ἐτῶν ὀγ. (Field, _Notes_, 49f.), [[Luk.2.37|Luk.2:37]] τ. ἐλθεῖν, [[Act.8.40|Act.8:40]] before names and events, [[Mat.1.17; 2.15|Mat.1:17 2:15]], [[Luk.11.51|Luk.11:51]], [[Jas.5.7|Jas.5:7]], al.;
(b) before οὗ, ὅτου, with the force of a _conjc._ (Burton, §330; M, _Pr._, 91);
(α) ἕ. οὗ (Hdt., ii, 143; Plut., al.): with indic., [[Mat.1.25|Mat.1:25]] (WH br., οὗ) 13:33, al.; with subjc. aor., [[Mat.14.22|Mat.14:22]], al.;
(β) ἔ. ὅτου: with subjc., [[Luk.13.8|Luk.13:8]] with indic., [[Mat.5.25|Mat.5:25]] (**until**), [[Jhn.9.18|Jhn.9:18]]
(with) with _adv._ (ἔ. ὀψέ, Thuc, iii, 108): ἄρτι, [[Mat.11.12|Mat.11:12]], [[Jhn.2.10|Jhn.2:10]], [[1Co.4.13|1Co.4:13]], al.; πότε (M, _Pr._, 107), [[Mat.17.17|Mat.17:17]], [[Mrk.9.19|Mrk.9:19]], [[Jhn.10.24|Jhn.10:24]], al.
2. Of place, **as far as, even to, unto** (Arist., al.);
(a) as _prep._ with genitive (see supr.): Mt 1123, Lk 1015, al.;
(b) with _adv._ (BL, §40, 6): ἄνω, [[Jhn.2.7|Jhn.2:7]] ἔσω, [[Mrk.14.54|Mrk.14:54]] κάτω, [[Mat.27.51|Mat.27:51]], [[Mrk.15.38|Mrk.15:38]]; ὧδε, [[Luk.23.5|Luk.23:5]]
(with) with _prep._: ἔξω, [[Act.21.5|Act.21:5]] πρός, [[Luk.24.50|Luk.24:50]] (Field, _Notes_, 83).
3. Of quantity, measure, etc.: [[Mat.18.21|Mat.18:21]], [[Mrk.6.23|Mrk.6:23]], [[Luk.22.51|Luk.22:51]], al.
(AS)

G2192.def:
**ἔχω**,
[in LXX for אָצֵל (ἐχόμενος), יֵשׁ,בַּעַל, etc., 59 words in all ;]
(on the _Aktionsart_ of the various tenses, see M, _Pr._, 110, 145, 150, 183), **to have**, as in cl., in various senses and constructions.
I. Trans.;
1. 1. **to have, hold, hold fast**, etc.;
(a) **to hold**, **as, in the hand**: [[Rev.5.8; 14.6|Rev.5:8 14:6]], al.; ἐν τ. χειρί, [[Rev.1.16; 10.2|Rev.1:16 10:2]], al.;
(b) of arms and clothing, = φέρω, φορέω, **to bear, wear**: [[Mat.3.4; 22.12|Mat.3:4 22:12]], al.; so frequently present ptcp. (LS, see word, A, I, 6; Bl., 74, 2), [[Mrk.11.13|Mrk.11:13]], [[Jhn.18.10|Jhn.18:10]], [[Rev.9.17|Rev.9:17]], al.;
(with) of a woman, ἐν γαστρὶ ἔ, **to be with child**: [[Mrk.13.17|Mrk.13:17]], [[Rom.9.10|Rom.9:10]];
(d) **to hold fast, keep**: [[Luk.19.20|Luk.19:20]] metaphorically, of the mind and conduct, [[Mrk.16.8|Mrk.16:8]] (cf. [[Job.21.6|Job.21:6]], [[Isa.13.8|Isa.13:8]]; Deiss., _BS_, 293; Field, _Notes_, 44f.), [[Jhn.14.21|Jhn.14:21]], [[Rom.1.28|Rom.1:28]], [[1Ti.3.9|1Ti.3:9]], [[2Ti.1.13|2Ti.1:13]], [[Rev.6.9|Rev.6:9]], al.;
(e) **to involve**: [[Heb.10.35|Heb.10:35]] (LXX), [[Jas.1.4|Jas.1:4]], [[1Jn.4.18|1Jn.4:18]] (_f_) = Lat. habere (Bl., §34, 5; 73, 5), **to hold, consider**: with accusative and predic. ptcp., [[Luk.14.18|Luk.14:18]] with accusative, before ὡς, [[Mat.14.5|Mat.14:5]] εἰς (Hebraism), [[Mat.21.46|Mat.21:46]] on (Bl., §70, 2), [[Mrk.11.32|Mrk.11:32]]
2. **to have, possess**;
(a) in general, with accusative of thing(s): [[Mat.19.22|Mat.19:22]], [[Mrk.10.22|Mrk.10:22]], [[Luk.12.19|Luk.12:19]], [[Jhn.10.16|Jhn.10:16]], [[1Co.11.22|1Co.11:22]], al.; of wealth or poverty, absol., ἔχειν (neg. οὐκ, μή), [[Mat.13.12; 25.29|Mat.13:12 25:29]], [[2Co.8.12|2Co.8:12]]; ἐκ τ. ἔχειν, **according to your means**, [[2Co.8.11|2Co.8:11]]
(b) of relationship, association, and: πατέρα, [[Jhn.8.41|Jhn.8:41]] γυναῖκα (MM, xiv), [[1Co.7.2|1Co.7:2]] φίλον, [[Luk.11.5|Luk.11:5]] βασιλέα, [[Jhn.19.15|Jhn.19:15]] ποιμένα, [[Mat.9.36|Mat.9:36]] with dupl. accusative, [[Mat.3.9|Mat.3:9]], al.;
(with) **of parts or members**: ὦτα, [[Mat.19.15|Mat.19:15]] μέλη, [[Rom.12.4|Rom.12:4]] θεμελίους,
(d) with accusative, as periphrasis of verb: μνεῖαν ἔ. (= μεμνῆσθαι), [[1Th.3.6|1Th.3:6]] ἀγάπην, [[Jhn.13.35|Jhn.13:35]] γνῶσιν, [[1Co.8.1|1Co.8:1]] πεποίθησιν, [[2Co.3.4|2Co.3:4]] θλίψιν, [[Jhn.16.33|Jhn.16:33]], etc. (Thayer, see word, I, 2, f., g.);
(e) of duty, necessity, etc.: ἀνάγκην, [[1Co.7.37|1Co.7:37]] νόμον, [[Jhn.19.7|Jhn.19:7]] ἐπιταγήν, [[1Co.7.25|1Co.7:25]] ἀγῶνα, [[Php.1.30|Php.1:30]] κρίμα, [[1Ti.5.12|1Ti.5:12]]
(f) **of complaints and disputes**; κατά, with genitive of person(s), [[Mat.5.23|Mat.5:23]], [[Mrk.11.25|Mrk.11:25]]; id. before ὅτι, [[Rev.2.4, 20|Rev.2:4, 20]]; with accusative before πρός, [[Act.24.19|Act.24:19]], al.;
(g) with inf.,
(α) (cl.) **to be able** (Field, _Notes_, 14): [[Mat.18.25|Mat.18:25]], [[Mrk.14.8|Mrk.14:8]] (sc. ποιῆσαι), [[Luk.12.4|Luk.12:4]], [[Act.4.14|Act.4:14]], al;
(β) **of necessity **(BL, §69, 4): [[Luk.12.50|Luk.12:50]], [[Act.23.17-19; 28.19|Act.23:17-19 28:19]].
II. Intrans. (BL, §53, 1), **to be in a certain condition**: ἑτοίμως ἔ., with inf., [[Act.21.13|Act.21:13]], [[2Co.12.14|2Co.12:14]]; ἐσχάτως (which see), [[Mrk.5.23|Mrk.5:23]] κακῶς, **to be ill**, [[Mat.4.24|Mat.4:24]], al.; καλῶς, Mk 16:[18]; κομψότερον, [[Jhn.4.52|Jhn.4:52]] πῶς, [[Act.15.36|Act.15:36]] impers., ἄλλως εἴχει, **it is otherwise**, [[1Ti.5.25|1Ti.5:25]] οὕτως, [[Act.7.1|Act.7:1]], al.; τὸ νῦν ἔχον, **as things now are** ([[Tob.7.11|Tob.7:11]]), [[Act.24.25|Act.24:25]].
III. Mid., -ομαι, **to hold oneself fast, hold on** or **cling to, be next to**: with genitive, τ. ἐχόμενα σωτηρίας, [[Heb.6.9|Heb.6:9]] (Rendall, in l.); ptcp., ὁ ἐχόμενος, **near, next**: of place, [[Mrk.1.38|Mrk.1:38]] of time, τ. ἐχομένη (ἡμέρα, expressed or understood), [[Luk.13.33|Luk.13:33]], [[Act.20.15; 21.26|Act.20:15 21:26]]; (σαββάτῳ), [[Act.13.44|Act.13:44]] (Cf. ἀν-, προσ-αν-, ἀντ-, ἀπ-, ἐν-, ἐπ-, κατ-, μετ-, παρ-, περι-, προ-, προσ-, συν-, ὑπερ-, ὑπ-έχω.)
(AS)

G2106.def:
**εὐ-δοκέω**, -ῶ
(on the derivation, see EL, § 28, 6) [in LXX chiefly for רָצָה, also for אָבָה, חָפֵץ, etc. ;]
1. with inf. (Polyb., al.), **to be well pleased, to think it good, to give consent **(so frequently in π. in legal docu­ments; Milligan, _Th._, 22 f.): [[Luk.12.32|Luk.12:32]], [[Rom.15.26-27|Rom.15:26-27]], [[1Co.1.21|1Co.1:21]], [[Gal.1.15|Gal.1:15]], [[Col.1.19|Col.1:19]], R, mg. (_ICC_, in l, but see infr.), [[1Th.2.8; 3.1|1Th.2:8 3:1]]; μᾶλλον εὐ., [[2Co.5.8|2Co.5:8]] with accusative and inf. (Polyb., i, 8, 4), Col, l.with, R, txt. (Lft., in l).
2. **to be well pleased or take pleasure with or in a person or thing**;
(a) with dative (Polyb., al.; [[1Ma.1.43|1Ma.1:43]], I [[Est.4.39|Est.4:39]]): [[2Th.2.12|2Th.2:12]];
(b) as frequently in LXX,
α with accusative: [[Mat.12.13|Mat.12:13]], [[Heb.10.5|Heb.10:5]], 8" (LXX) ;
β before ἐν (cf. _Heb._ בּ רָצָה, [[Psa.149.4|Psa.149:4]]): [[Mat.3.17; 17.5|Mat.3:17 17:5]], [[Mrk.1.11|Mrk.1:11]], [[Luk.3.22|Luk.3:22]] (on the tense, see M, _Pr._, 134 f.; _DCG_, i,308 b), [[1Co.10.5|1Co.10:5]], [[2Co.12.10|2Co.12:10]], [[Heb.10.38|Heb.10:38]]" (LXX) ;
(with) before εἰς: [[2Pe.1.17|2Pe.1:17]] (cf. συν-ευδοκέω, and see Cremer, 213 f.; Field, _Notes_, 48 f.; _DCG_, i, 355a.)†
(AS)

G2186.def:
**ἐφ-ίστημι **
[in LXX for נָצַב ni., שִׁית, נָתַן, etc. ;]
1. causal in pres., impf., fut., 1 aor., to set upon or by, set up, etc. (Æsch., Hdt., Arist., al).
2. Intrans. in mid, and in pf. and 2 aor. act.;
(a) **to stand upon**;
(b) **to be set over**;
(with) **to stand by, be present, be at hand, come on or upon**: [[Luk.2.38; 10.40; 20.1|Luk.2:38 10:40 20:1]], [[Act.6.12; 12.7; 22.13, 20; 23.27|Act.6:12 12:7 22:13, 20 23:27]], [[2Ti.4.2|2Ti.4:2]]; with dative pars., [[Luk.2.9; 24.4|Luk.2:9 24:4]], [[Act.4.1; 23.11|Act.4:1 23:11]]; with dative bc., [[Act.17.5|Act.17:5]] before έπί, with accusative, [[Act.10.17; 11.11|Act.10:17 11:11]]; of rain, [[Act.28.2|Act.28:2]] of evils impending, with dative of person(s), [[1Th.5.3|1Th.5:3]] before έπί ([[Wis.6.9|Wis.6:9]]), [[Luk.21.34|Luk.21:34]]; of time, [[2Ti.4.6|2Ti.4:6]] (cf. κατ-, συν-εφίστημι).†
(AS)
